course: dictionary
lesson: 13904
title: Comparing with larger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Larger is the comparative of large. Use it when you compare two things: if one is large and the other is larger, the larger one is bigger. «The red box is larger than the blue box.» Here larger tells you the red box is the bigger of the two.
explain: Larger is not only for things you can touch. Numbers can be larger too. «Which is the larger number, 58 or 85?» 85 is more than 58, so 85 is the larger number. In fractions, a larger part means more of the whole.
explain: Sometimes larger has a special meaning. «Grandad is larger than life.» This phrase means very lively and exciting, not physically bigger. When you meet a phrase with a word you know, check the words around it to see if the meaning is simple or special.
fact: Larger means bigger than another one.
fact: Use larger when you compare two things. Large, larger, largest: largest is for three or more.
fact: A larger number is one that is more than another number: 9 is larger than 6.
fact: «Larger than life» means very lively and exciting.
fact: Some things can be larger in size, like a pizza, a drink, or a planet. «A larger pizza» means a bigger pizza than the other one.
exercise: «The red ball is larger than the green ball.» Which ball is bigger? | Neither ball is round | Both balls are the same size | The green ball | *The red ball
exercise: Which is the larger number: 58 or 85? | *85 | 58 | They are equal | Neither number
exercise: «Grandad is larger than life.» What does larger than life mean? | Very tall and heavy | Hard to see | Lost in a crowd | *Very lively and exciting
test: «A larger pizza has more slices than a small one.» What does larger mean here? | Sour and sharp | Hidden under a plate | *Bigger than a small one | Colder
test: Which fraction is larger, one half or one quarter? | One quarter | Neither is a fraction | *One half | They are the same
exam: «Ella has a larger bag than Sam, and Sam has a larger bag than Joe.» Whose bag is the smallest? | Ella | Sam | Nobody, they are all the same | *Joe
